      "math_academy_id": "e-10356",
      "problem": "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14198179/assets/44884515beb663ea65e292341857bb13ef6a6027572b811a1c5df2eae4def4ec.svg)\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS = [0,1] \\times [2,3].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y) = g(x) \\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x) =\\dfrac{3}{5} \\sqrt{x}$ and $h(y) =y.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 0.$",
